## Audit done — and one thing needs your decision before anything can be implemented

**Artifact:** `audit/orchestration-surface-audit.md` (in this workspace).

### What I found

**The bundle isn't here.** This session's workspace is empty; the bundle is `/root/dshProj/my-power-dsh` (branch `fix/todo-register-p1`, dirty tree). I can **read** it, but writes fail with `Read-only file system` — so nothing can land in the bundle from this session regardless of what the change turns out to be. It also has a **live running wave** (`friction-p1-wave`, 70 tasks, 1 pending) enforcing "ONE git writer" and exclusive `inScope`, plus a second running team.

**Orchestration surface** = `packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/` (adopted `@nanmicoder/dsh-agent-teams`, declared `0.1.16-rc.3-mpd`): `tools.js` 215 KB, `mpd-deltas.js` 232 KB, `state.js`, `quality-gates.js`, `scheduler.js`, `members.js`, `session-start.js`, `client.js` — seven of them edited today by the live wave.

**Upstream alignment — there are two upstreams, not one:**
- `oh-my-openagent` — sha-pinned in `VENDOR_LOCK.json` (`8c57e463…`, v5.0.0-beta.20), gated by `verify-vendor.mjs`.
- `dsh-agent-teams` — the adopted plugin. Measured drift: upstream HEAD `502dd6c` is **exactly one commit** past tag `v0.1.16-rc.3` (`cca92ae`), and that commit is **docs-only**. So the adopted body is aligned to rc.3; alignment is partial *by design* (0.1.14 body + audited backported deltas).
